# Copy to .env for local dev if you need to point at a non-default API (rare
# — the Vite dev server proxies /api to localhost:4000 by default, see
# vite.config.ts, so most local dev needs no .env at all).
#
# REQUIRED for a real deployment where the frontend and API are on
# different origins (e.g. this app on Cloudflare Pages, API on its own
# domain) — set as a build-time environment variable in the Cloudflare
# Pages project settings, not a checked-in file. Without it, apiClient.ts
# falls back to the relative path "/api", which only works when the
# frontend is served from the same origin as the API.
VITE_API_URL=https://api.yourdomain.com/api
